# ============================================================================
# Cloudflare Pages Environment Variables
# ============================================================================
# This file contains all environment variables required for deploying
# PT2030 Candidaturas to Cloudflare Pages.
#
# IMPORTANT:
# - All client-side variables MUST start with VITE_ prefix (Vite requirement)
# - Copy this file and set actual values in Cloudflare Pages dashboard
# - Go to: Pages → pt2030-candidaturas → Settings → Environment Variables
#
# Setup Instructions:
# 1. Copy values from your current .env file
# 2. Add each variable in Cloudflare Pages settings
# 3. Set variables for both "Production" and "Preview" environments
# 4. Redeploy after adding/changing variables
# ============================================================================

# ============================================================================
# REQUIRED VARIABLES
# ============================================================================
# These variables are required for the application to function properly.
# The deployment will fail if these are not set.

# Supabase Configuration
# Get these from: https://supabase.com/dashboard → Your Project → Settings → API
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...

# ============================================================================
# OPTIONAL BUT RECOMMENDED VARIABLES
# ============================================================================
# These variables enable additional features but app will work without them.

# OpenRouter API Configuration
# Used for AI-powered features (proposal generation, AI assistance)
# Get your API key from: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# Leave empty to disable AI features
VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY=sk-or-v1-...

# Public URL
# The public-facing URL of your application
# For Cloudflare Pages, this will be one of:
# - Production: https://pt2030-candidaturas.pages.dev
# - Custom domain: https://your-domain.com
# - Preview: https://[branch].pt2030-candidaturas.pages.dev
VITE_PUBLIC_URL=https://pt2030-candidaturas.pages.dev

# ============================================================================
# MONITORING & ANALYTICS
# ============================================================================
# These variables enable error tracking, analytics, and observability.
# Recommended for production, optional for preview deployments.

# Sentry Configuration
# Error tracking and performance monitoring
# Get your DSN from: https://sentry.io/ → Your Project → Settings → Client Keys
# Format: https://[key]@[org].ingest.sentry.io/[project-id]
VITE_SENTRY_DSN=https://your_key@your_org.ingest.sentry.io/your_project_id

# Sentry Build Configuration (for source maps upload)
# Only needed if you want to upload source maps during build
# Get auth token from: https://sentry.io/settings/account/api/auth-tokens/
# Set these in Cloudflare Pages build environment variables
SENTRY_AUTH_TOKEN=sntrys_your_auth_token_here
SENTRY_ORG=your_sentry_org_slug
SENTRY_PROJECT=pt2030-candidaturas

# PostHog Configuration
# Product analytics and user behavior tracking
# Get your key from: https://app.posthog.com/project/settings
# For EU GDPR compliance, use EU instance: https://eu.posthog.com
VITE_POSTHOG_KEY=phc_your_posthog_key_here

# ============================================================================
# CLOUDFLARE-SPECIFIC SETTINGS
# ============================================================================
# These are automatically set by Cloudflare Pages and don't need manual configuration

# Node.js Version
# Set in cloudflare-pages.toml: NODE_VERSION = "18"
# NODE_VERSION=18

# Environment
# Automatically set by Cloudflare Pages:
# - "production" for production branch (main)
# - "preview" for preview deployments
# CF_PAGES_BRANCH=main
# CF_PAGES_COMMIT_SHA=abc123
# CF_PAGES_URL=https://pt2030-candidaturas.pages.dev

# ============================================================================
# ENVIRONMENT-SPECIFIC CONFIGURATIONS
# ============================================================================
# Configure different values for Production vs Preview environments in Cloudflare dashboard

# Production Environment:
# - Use production Supabase project
# - Use production API keys
# - Enable all monitoring (Sentry, PostHog)
# - Use production OpenRouter quota

# Preview Environment (optional):
# - Use staging/test Supabase project (if available)
# - Use development API keys with lower rate limits
# - Optionally disable monitoring to save quota
# - Use separate OpenRouter project for testing

# ============================================================================
# SECURITY NOTES
# ============================================================================
# ⚠️  IMPORTANT SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS:
#
# 1. Client-Side Exposure:
#    - All VITE_* variables are exposed to the client browser
#    - Never put secret keys in VITE_* variables
#    - Only use public/anonymous keys (like Supabase anon key)
#
# 2. Server-Side Secrets:
#    - For true secrets, use Cloudflare Workers/Functions
#    - Store secrets in Cloudflare Workers secrets (not env vars)
#    - Never commit actual values to Git
#
# 3. API Keys:
#    - Supabase anon key: ✅ Safe for client (RLS protects data)
#    - OpenRouter API key: ⚠️  Use with rate limiting/quotas
#    - Sentry DSN: ✅ Safe for client (public identifier)
#    - PostHog key: ✅ Safe for client (public identifier)
#
# 4. Domain Restrictions:
#    - Configure allowed origins in Supabase dashboard
#    - Set up CORS properly for APIs
#    - Use Cloudflare Access for additional protection
#
# ============================================================================
# SETTING VARIABLES IN CLOUDFLARE PAGES
# ============================================================================
#
# Via Dashboard:
# 1. Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com/
# 2. Select your account
# 3. Click "Pages" → "pt2030-candidaturas"
# 4. Go to "Settings" → "Environment variables"
# 5. Click "Add variable"
# 6. Enter variable name and value
# 7. Select environment: Production, Preview, or Both
# 8. Click "Save"
# 9. Redeploy for changes to take effect
#
# Via Wrangler CLI:
# wrangler pages secret put VARIABLE_NAME --project-name=pt2030-candidaturas
# (Then paste the value when prompted)
#
# Bulk Import (from .env file):
# Currently not supported directly - must add each variable manually
#
# ============================================================================
# VERIFICATION
# ============================================================================
# After setting variables, verify they're loaded correctly:
#
# 1. Trigger a new deployment
# 2. Check build logs for any missing variable warnings
# 3. Test the deployed app in browser
# 4. Open browser console and check:
#    console.log(import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL)
#    Should show your Supabase URL (not 'undefined')
#
# ============================================================================
# TROUBLESHOOTING
# ============================================================================
#
# Q: Variables showing as 'undefined' in browser?
# A: Make sure variable name starts with VITE_ and is set in Cloudflare Pages
#
# Q: Changes not taking effect?
# A: Trigger a new deployment after changing variables
#
# Q: Different values for staging vs production?
# A: Set different values for "Production" vs "Preview" environments
#
# Q: How to keep secrets secret?
# A: Don't use VITE_ prefix for secrets, use Cloudflare Workers instead
#
# ============================================================================
# MIGRATION FROM RAILWAY
# ============================================================================
# If migrating from Railway, map variables as follows:
#
# Railway Variable          → Cloudflare Variable
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SUPABASE_URL             → VITE_SUPABASE_URL
# SUPABASE_ANON_KEY        → VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY       → VITE_OPENROUTER_API_KEY
# PORT                     → (not needed)
# NODE_ENV                 → (auto-set to 'production')
#
# Note: Add VITE_ prefix to all variables that need to be accessible in browser
# ============================================================================

